items.prompt:
A desk's 99% one-day VaR had 9 breaches over the last 250 trading days, all in March. The VaR is a normal VaR built on a 250-day sample sd.

Write a note to the risk committee (about 250 words). Cover:

(a) the count against what a correct model gives, with the numbers;

(b) Kupiec's test and Basel's traffic light;

(c) what the March clustering means;

(d) the changes you propose, and how you would check them;

(e) one limit of these tests.
